<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT -Banco Frances started.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT -Banco Frances started.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Credit Lyonnais Securities analysts Victoria Munoz and Andrew Collins have started coverage of Argentina's Banco Frances with a rating of hold.</p>
<p>-- In a May 2 report, they set a 14-month price target of $35.50 per American Depositary Receipt (ADR).</p>
<p>-- &quot;Frances has historically traded at a premium to the Argentine market and we forecast that it will continue to do so, due to its high level of solvency, liquidity and profitability.&quot;</p>
<p>-- ADRs in the company were off 1/8 to 30.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
